NAME "JDT fluid drop"

-- Just Dire Things fluid drop recipes (catalyst item dropped into fluid B -> fluid C),
-- fed by an AE2 pattern provider. One craft at a time, exact amounts:
-- 1 item + 1000 mB per cycle, so a pattern for N crafts just runs N cycles.
--
-- Labels:
--   src       chest + tank next to the pattern provider (provider pushes into both; blocking mode ON)
--   provider  the pattern provider (inserting into it returns the result to ME)
--   placer    Fluid Placer, redstone mode Ignored
--   dropper   Dropper, redstone mode Ignored
--   collector Fluid Collector, redstone mode High
--   idle, armed, gate   three empty chests; ONE token item (any item) starts in idle.
--                        Comparator off gate -> collector, so it only runs while the token sits there.
-- Placer, dropper and collector all face the same empty block.
--
-- SFM can't emit redstone, and an ungated collector grabs fluid B before the catalyst lands.
-- The token remembers the phase; the IFs run gate -> armed -> idle so each step waits a full tick.

EVERY 20 TICKS DO
    -- 3. fluid C collected: send it home, back to idle
    IF gate HAS GE 1 AND collector HAS GE 1000 fluid:: THEN
        INPUT fluid:: FROM collector
        OUTPUT fluid:: TO provider
        FORGET
        INPUT FROM gate
        OUTPUT TO idle
        FORGET
    END

    -- 2. fluid placed and catalyst dropped: let the collector loose
    IF armed HAS GE 1 AND placer HAS EQ 0 fluid:: AND dropper HAS EQ 0 THEN
        INPUT FROM armed
        OUTPUT TO gate
        FORGET
    END

    -- 1. a craft is waiting and the machines are clear: load exactly one
    IF
        idle HAS GE 1
        AND src HAS GE 1000 fluid::
        AND src HAS GE 1
        AND placer HAS EQ 0 fluid::
        AND dropper HAS EQ 0
    THEN
        INPUT 1000 fluid:: FROM src
        OUTPUT fluid:: TO placer
        FORGET
        INPUT 1 FROM src
        OUTPUT TO dropper
        FORGET
        INPUT FROM idle
        OUTPUT TO armed
        FORGET
    END
END
